        <item>
            <title>Version 1.2.0</title>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <style>
                    :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
                    body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; line-height: 1.45; margin: 4px 2px; }
                    h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
                    h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 16px 0 4px; }
                    p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
                    ol, ul { margin: 0 0 8px; padding-left: 20px; }
                    li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
                    .muted { opacity: 0.7; }
                </style>
                <h2>🫥 New: Blur Screen</h2>
                <p>Step away from your Mac without leaving your inbox, messages or code on display.</p>
                <p>With <b>Blur Screen</b> turned on, HammerTime covers every display with frosted glass while it's active. People walking by can't read your screen, and HammerTime still catches anyone who touches your Mac.</p>
                <h3>How to turn it on</h3>
                <ol>
                    <li>Click the 🔨 in the menu bar and open <b>Settings</b>.</li>
                    <li>Under <b>While Active</b>, switch on <b>Blur Screen</b>.</li>
                    <li>Click <b>Preview</b> to see what others will see.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="muted">Off by default, so your lock stays invisible unless you turn it on. No new permissions needed.</p>
                <h3>✨ Also in this update</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>A tidier Settings window: Blur Screen and Touch ID now sit together under <b>While Active</b>.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
